            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Latin for ownership, then the Latin for formal purchase."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: aes aliēnum, aeris aliēnī",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aes aliēnum, aeris aliēnī — \"debt\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Aere aliēnō premitur. He is weighed down by debt."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aes aliēnum, aeris aliēnī n.: other people's bronze, money that belongs to someone else. In aere aliēnō esse, to be in debt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aes aliēnum is built from aes \"bronze, money\" and aliēnus \"belonging to another\" (Lewis & Short): money that is someone else's."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
