          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "fēnus is usually traced to a root meaning \"to bring forth, to yield\", the root Lewis & Short also see in fēmina: what money produces. The account is not certain."
            }
          ]
        },
